  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #2748 (issue #2744) makes the report door send the file name of the project, not the path. It replaces the exact project path in the status line too.\n\nThe status line can hold a different path, for example the path of an export or of a posted file. The shared report keeps that path. The path can have the user name in it, and the browser sends it to github.com in the URL.\n\n## Source\n\nThe worker of #2744 reported this limit. No test shows it.\n\n## What should happen\n\n- The shared report does not include a directory part from the status line. One option: the shared report omits the status line or keeps only its message text.\n- A test pins this with a status line that names an export path in a user directory.\n\nRefs #2744\n",
